@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
title Notification Methods collaboration boundary
component "Test inputs\nand assertions" as Test
rectangle "Declared real collaboration SUT" {
 component "ReaderNotificationController" as Controller
 component "LendingServiceImpl\n(periodic check and dispatch)" as Lending
 component "Channel composition" as Composition
 component "Reader preference\nvalidation and storage" as Preferences
 component "Notification Service" as Service
 component "ReaderRepository" as Repo
 Controller --> Preferences
 Composition --> Lending
 Lending --> Service
 Lending --> Repo
 Preferences --> Repo
 Service --> Repo
}
component "Local receivers\n(SMTP and HTTP, loopback only)" as Mechanism
component "Test properties\n(enabled channels)" as Props
component "Real clock, with dates\nrelative to today\n(outside SUT)" as Clock
database "Dedicated test DB\nwith known readers and preferences" as DB
Test --> Controller
Test --> Lending : run periodic check
Service --> Mechanism
Composition ..> Props : bound at startup
Lending --> Clock
Repo --> DB


note bottom of Service
  "Notification Service" in this graph is a stand-in
  for the different implementations of
  NotificationService that need their
  specific behaviour tested.
end note

note bottom of Mechanism
  Stands in for the specific notification channel protocols (SMS, e-mail, webhook (http/https)).
  It stays outside the SUT: 0 real messages (CON-TST-8).
end note
@enduml